<title>BELARUS: Belarus Belavia begins Minsk-Rome regular flights.</title>
<headline>Belarus Belavia begins Minsk-Rome regular flights.</headline>
<dateline>MINSK 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belarussian state-owned airline Belavia will begin scheduled passenger flights between Minsk and Rome as of June 6, a senior company official said on Friday.</p>
<p>Belavia commercial director Vasiliy Kornev told Reuters a Tupolev Tu-154 jet would service the twice-weekly flights.</p>
<p>&quot;Currently, Belavia operates scheduled flights and charters from Belarus to 21 countries,&quot; he said, adding the carrier plans to begin a regular service to China in July, which would likely fly from Minsk to Bejing.</p>
<p>He did not give further details.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
